Vendored build inputs for the Ubuntu PPA source package
========================================================

Launchpad's PPA builders have no network access, so the source package carries:

rustc / cargo / rust-std 1.97.1, for each architecture the package is built on:
    x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu   (amd64)
    aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu  (arm64)
    The official standalone component tarballs from
    https://static.rust-lang.org/dist/, unmodified. debian/rules runs each
    one's install.sh into debian/.rust, for the builder's own architecture.
    A build for an architecture whose three tarballs are missing fails with a
    message naming the missing toolchain.

crates-<version>.tar.xz
    Produced by ./packaging/vendor/make-crates.sh: `cargo vendor` of the whole
    workspace, with crates neither Linux architecture compiles replaced by
    stubs. The same tarball serves amd64 and arm64.
    Regenerate whenever Cargo.lock changes.

SHA256SUMS lists every one of those files; debian/rules verifies it before
building. make-crates.sh writes it from the tarballs found in this directory,
so download the rust tarballs of both architectures first. The tarballs are
gitignored but included in the source package.
